course: dictionary
lesson: 14751
title: Propagation: growing, spreading, and sharing
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Propagation is a science word, and it has three main meanings. In gardening, it means growing new plants from a parent plant, using seeds, cuttings or bulbs. «Mia cut a stem from her mint plant and put it in water to grow a new one.» That is plant propagation.
explain: In physics, propagation means spreading from one place to another. «Sound propagation through water is quicker than through air.» Here the sound is travelling, or spreading, through the water.
explain: In formal language, propagation means spreading ideas or beliefs. «The propagation of the rumour took only one lunch break.» Swap in the word spreading and check: the rumour spread around the school, so the meaning fits.
fact: Propagation is a noun. Its verb is propagate, which means to grow new plants or to spread something.
fact: «Plant propagation» means growing new plants from a parent plant.
fact: Cuttings, seeds and bulbs are common ways to propagate plants.
fact: «Propagation of sound» means how sound spreads from one place to another, through air, water or solids.
fact: In formal use, «propagation of ideas» means spreading ideas or beliefs from person to person.
exercise: «Mia grew a new mint plant from a cutting of her old one.» What is this process called? | *Propagation | Decoration | Pollution | Illumination
exercise: «Sound propagation through water is quick.» What does propagation mean here? | *Spreading from one place to another | Turning off the lights | Freezing into ice | Growing new plants from seeds
exercise: «The propagation of the rumour took one lunch break.» What does propagation mean? | Sleeping in the sun | Measuring how loud a sound is | Cutting a plant into pieces | *Spreading an idea or belief
test: Which is NOT a common way to propagate a plant? | Bulbs | Seeds | Cuttings | *Melting ice
test: Which sentence uses propagation to mean spreading ideas? | Ben planted bulbs in the pot. | *The propagation of the belief spread through the town. | The sound was heard in the next room.
exam: Which of these shows sound propagation? | A plant grows from a seed. | *Sound travels from a drum through the air to your ear. | Ice melts in the sun. | A cup breaks on the floor.
